IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`

-- g2-art7-public-benefit.l4: Article 7 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Public benefit: what the person who determines whether an entity provides, or intends to provide, public benefit
-- must have regard to and must not do.  Group G2.  Imports only prelude, daydate, domain and `g2-nouns`.  No section GIVEN.
--
-- "To a reasonable degree" (Article 5(1)(b)) is the DETERMINER'S finding, so it is an input: the record `Determination of public benefit` holds who determined, what was found, and what the determiner
-- did and did not do.  Article 7 does not compute public benefit; it constrains the determination.  Three consequences are encoded:
--   (1) Article 7(1) names only the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court as bound by paragraphs (2) and (3); Article 5(5) binds every determiner to have regard to the guidance.  FORK F2.13 (added after
--       independent testing) adds, on the first reading (taken), a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3).
--   (2) Article 7(3)(b) makes one outcome a matter of law and not of finding: an entity that benefits only one natural person or a group of identified natural persons is NOT treated as providing
--       public benefit, whatever the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court found.
--   (3) The Law does not say what follows from a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker.  FORK F2.10 names three readings; the first (taken) is that such a determination does not
--       answer the question, so the encoding refuses.

§ `Part 3 — Charity Test`

§§ `Article 7 — Public benefit`

-- A refusal, named for what it says, because the Law does not say what follows from a breach by the maker of a determination.
@ref Article 7(1) to 7(3) and Article 5(5) (src:157) (src:203-212)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit` MEANS
    REFUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `Article 7(1) — To whom paragraphs (2) and (3) apply`

-- src:203 | (1) Paragraphs (2) and (3) apply to the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court when determining the question of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit, for the purpose of Article 5(1)(b).
-- src:795 | (2) To the extent that any States’ employee (within the meaning of the Employment of States of Jersey Employees (Jersey) Law 2005), while made available under sub-paragraph (1), performs a function under the direction of the Commissioner, the employee is to be treated as a member of the Commissioner’s staff for the purposes of this Law.
-- src:796 | (3) Any function of the Commissioner may, to the extent authorized by the Commissioner, be exercised on behalf of the Commissioner by any member of the Commissioner’s staff, except –

-- FORK F2.13 (added after independent testing): is a member of the Commissioner's staff, exercising a function of the Commissioner, bound as the Commissioner is?  Article 7(1) names the
-- Commissioner, the tribunal and the court, and no one else; Article 5(5) names the Commissioner, the tribunal, a registered charity and a governor of a registered charity.  But Schedule 1
-- paragraph 4(3) lets any function of the Commissioner be exercised on the Commissioner's behalf by a member of staff, to the extent the Commissioner authorizes, and a function so exercised
-- is the Commissioner's function: the duties that attach to it go with it, and otherwise authorizing staff would take a determination out of Article 7(3)(b).  That is the first reading
-- (taken).  The second reading binds only the persons the Articles name, so a determination by staff is a determination by "anyone else".  The constructor `a member of the Commissioner's
-- staff` stands for a member of staff exercising a function of the Commissioner under that authority; a member of staff acting otherwise is recorded as `any person`.
@ref Article 7(1), Article 5(5), Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) (src:203) (src:157) (src:795-796)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 7(1) and 5(5) the Commissioner's staff are bound as the Commissioner is` interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound`
    WHEN `a member of staff exercising a function of the Commissioner under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) is bound as the Commissioner is`
        THEN `reading A of F2.13: a function exercised on the Commissioner's behalf carries the Commissioner's duties`
    WHEN `only the persons that Article 7(1) and Article 5(5) name are bound`
        THEN `reading B of F2.13: only the persons the Articles name are bound`

@ref Article 7(1), Article 5(5), Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) (src:203) (src:157) (src:795-796)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reading A of F2.13: a function exercised on the Commissioner's behalf carries the Commissioner's duties` MEANS
    TRUE

@ref Article 7(1), Article 5(5), Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) (src:203) (src:157) (src:795-796)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reading B of F2.13: only the persons the Articles name are bound` MEANS
    FALSE

@ref Article 7(1) (src:203)
@export Whether Article 7(2) and (3) bind a person who determines whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit: they bind the Commissioner, the Charity Tribunal and the court, and (on the first reading of fork F2.13) a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3), and no one else
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
        @desc The person who determines whether the entity provides or intends to provide public benefit
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` who interp MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `the Commissioner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Charity Tribunal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a member of the Commissioner's staff` THEN `Arts 7(1) and 5(5) the Commissioner's staff are bound as the Commissioner is` interp
    WHEN `the Minister` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the States` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Attorney General` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Bailiff` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Jersey Financial Services Commission` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Comptroller` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an applicant for registration` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a registered charity` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a governor` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any person` THEN FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `Article 7(2) — What the person determining must have regard to`

-- src:204 | (2) The person determining the question must have regard to –
-- src:205 | (a) how any –
-- src:206 | (i) benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or any other persons (other than as members of the public), and
-- src:207 | (ii) disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public,
-- src:208 | in consequence of the entity exercising its functions, compares with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public in that consequence; and
-- src:209 | (b) if benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only, whether any condition on obtaining that benefit (including any charge or fee) is unduly restrictive.

-- 7(2)(a) and (b) as facts about the determination: regard to the comparison of benefit and disbenefit; and, if benefit goes to a section of the public only, regard to whether any condition
-- on obtaining it is unduly restrictive.  The condition of (b) is a gate: where benefit is not so limited, (b) asks for nothing.
@ref Article 7(2) (src:204-209)
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7(2) the determiner had the regard that Article 7(2) requires` determination MEANS
        "(a)" ... determination's `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public`
    AND "(b)" ... (    NOT determination's `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only`
                    OR determination's `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive`)

-- The duty of 7(2)(a) as a regulative rule: the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court must have regard to the comparison.  It has no period; it is a standing duty.
@ref Article 7(2)(a) (src:205-208)
@export The standing duty under Article 7(2)(a) of the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court (and, on the first reading of fork F2.13, of a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function), when determining public benefit, to have regard to how benefit to members or others and disbenefit to the public compare with benefit to the public; it binds no one else
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
        @desc The person who determines whether the entity provides or intends to provide public benefit
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`Art 7(2)(a) the person determining must have regard to the comparison of benefit and disbenefit` who interp MEANS
    IF `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` who interp
    THEN PARTY who
         MUST `have regard to how benefit to members or other persons (other than as members of the public) and disbenefit to the public compare with benefit to the public` who
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The duty of 7(2)(b): only if benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only.
@ref Article 7(2)(b) (src:209)
@export The standing duty under Article 7(2)(b) of the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court (and, on the first reading of fork F2.13, of a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function), where benefit is or is likely to be provided to a section of the public only, to have regard to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including a charge or fee, is unduly restrictive
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
        @desc The person who determines whether the entity provides or intends to provide public benefit
      `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if the benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`Art 7(2)(b) the person determining must have regard to whether a condition on obtaining the benefit is unduly restrictive` who `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` interp MEANS
    IF `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` who interp AND `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only`
    THEN PARTY who
         MUST `have regard to whether any condition on obtaining a benefit provided to a section of the public only, including a charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` who
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `Article 7(3) — What the person determining must not do`

-- src:210 | (3) The person determining the question must not –
-- src:211 | (a) presume any particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit; or
-- src:212 | (b) treat one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons as being a section of the public, and accordingly must not treat an entity that benefits only such a person or persons as providing public benefit.

-- 7(3)(a): must not presume any particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit.
@ref Article 7(3)(a) (src:211)
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7(3)(a) the determination did not presume a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` determination MEANS
    NOT determination's `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit`

-- 7(3)(b): must not treat one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons as a section of the public, "and accordingly" must not treat an entity that benefits only such
-- a person or persons as providing public benefit.  Two limbs: the conduct, and the outcome that follows from it.  A positive finding that the entity provides, or intends to provide, public
-- benefit is treating it as providing it.
@ref Article 7(3)(b) (src:212)
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7(3)(b) the determination did not treat identified natural persons as a section of the public` determination MEANS
        NOT determination's `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public`
    AND NOT (    determination's `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons`
             AND (    determination's `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`
                  OR determination's `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`))

@ref Article 7(1), Article 7(3) (src:203) (src:210-212)
@export Whether a determination of public benefit is permitted by Article 7(3): it presumed no charitable purpose to be for the public benefit and did not treat identified natural persons as a section of the public; the paragraph binds the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court (and, on the first reading of fork F2.13, a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function), so it is satisfied vacuously by any other determiner
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
        @desc The determination: who made it, what it found, and what its maker did and did not do
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` determination interp MEANS
        (NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` (determination's `who made the determination`) interp)
    OR  (    `Art 7(3)(a) the determination did not presume a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` determination
         AND `Art 7(3)(b) the determination did not treat identified natural persons as a section of the public` determination)

-- The prohibitions of 7(3) as regulative rules.  Neither names a period, so each holds without end ("SHANT ... WITHIN n sunsets at n").
@ref Article 7(3)(a) (src:211)
@export The standing prohibition under Article 7(3)(a) on the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court (and, on the first reading of fork F2.13, on a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function) presuming any particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit; it binds no one else
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
        @desc The person who determines whether the entity provides or intends to provide public benefit
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`Art 7(3)(a) the person determining must not presume a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` who interp MEANS
    IF `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` who interp
    THEN PARTY who
         SHANT `presume a particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` who
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "Article 7(3)(a): the person determining presumed a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref Article 7(3)(b) (src:212)
@export The standing prohibition under Article 7(3)(b) on the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court (and, on the first reading of fork F2.13, on a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function) treating one natural person or a group of identified natural persons as a section of the public; it binds no one else
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
        @desc The person who determines whether the entity provides or intends to provide public benefit
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`Art 7(3)(b) the person determining must not treat identified natural persons as a section of the public` who interp MEANS
    IF `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` who interp
    THEN PARTY who
         SHANT `treat one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons as a section of the public` who
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "Article 7(3)(b): the person determining treated identified natural persons as a section of the public"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref Article 7(3)(b) (src:212)
@export The standing prohibition under Article 7(3)(b) on the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court (and, on the first reading of fork F2.13, on a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function) treating an entity that benefits only one natural person or a group of identified natural persons as providing public benefit; it binds no one else
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
        @desc The person who determines whether the entity provides or intends to provide public benefit
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`Art 7(3)(b) the person determining must not treat an entity that benefits only identified natural persons as providing public benefit` who interp MEANS
    IF `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` who interp
    THEN PARTY who
         SHANT `treat an entity that benefits only one natural person or a group of identified natural persons as providing public benefit` who
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "Article 7(3)(b): the person determining treated an entity that benefits only identified natural persons as providing public benefit"
    ELSE FULFILLED

