§§§ `Article 7 — Whether the entity provides public benefit, on a determination`

-- src:157 | (5) Any person, in determining whether an entity meets the charity test, must have regard to the guidance, and the Commissioner, the tribunal, a registered charity and a governor of a registered charity must have regard to the guidance when performing any other of their functions under this Law to which the guidance is relevant.
-- Whether the determination was made as the Law requires of its maker: every determiner must have regard to the guidance (Article 5(5)); the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court must also
-- have the regard that 7(2) requires and respect 7(3).
@ref Article 5(5), Article 7(1) to 7(3) (src:157) (src:203-212)
@export Whether a determination of public benefit complies with the duties on its maker: regard to the guidance (Article 5(5)) for every maker, and for the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court (and, on the first reading of fork F2.13, a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function) also the regard Article 7(2) requires and the restraints of Article 7(3)
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
        @desc The determination: who made it, what it found, and what its maker did and did not do
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` determination interp MEANS
        determination's `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)`
    AND (    NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` (determination's `who made the determination`) interp
         OR (    `Art 7(2) the determiner had the regard that Article 7(2) requires` determination
             AND `Art 7(3) the determination is permitted` determination interp))

-- src:149 | (b) in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree.
-- The finding: Article 5(1)(b) asks whether the entity provides public benefit and, in the case of an applicant, whether it provides or intends to provide it.
@ref Article 5(1)(b) (src:149)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
      `the public benefit determination` IS A `Determination of public benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7 the determination finds public benefit as Article 5(1)(b) asks` `the entity` `the public benefit determination` MEANS
        `the public benefit determination`'s `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`
    OR  (    `the entity`'s `standing on the register` EQUALS `an applicant for registration`
         AND `the public benefit determination`'s `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`)

-- Whether the entity provides public benefit, in the sense of Article 5(1)(b), on a determination.
--   * Article 7(3)(b): an entity that benefits only identified natural persons is not treated as providing public benefit by the Commissioner, the tribunal or the court, whatever they found.
--   * A determination that complies with the duties on its maker answers with its finding.
--   * One that does not: the Law does not say what follows.  FORK F2.10: it does not answer (taken); the finding stands; the entity is treated as not providing public benefit.
@ref Article 5(1)(b), Article 7 (src:149) (src:203-213)
@export Whether the entity provides public benefit (or, for an applicant, provides or intends to provide it) to a reasonable degree, on a determination by the Commissioner, the tribunal, the court or anyone else; a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker is treated as the interpretation says
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is what follows from a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
        @desc The entity as Article 2 leaves it; its standing on the register says whether it is an applicant
      `the public benefit determination` IS A `Determination of public benefit`
        @desc The determination: who made it, what it found, and what its maker did and did not do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` interp `the entity` `the public benefit determination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` (`the public benefit determination`'s `who made the determination`) interp
           AND `the public benefit determination`'s `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons`
        THEN FALSE
        IF `Art 7 the determination complies with the duties on its maker` `the public benefit determination` interp
        THEN `Art 7 the determination finds public benefit as Article 5(1)(b) asks` `the entity` `the public benefit determination`
        OTHERWISE `Art 7 a determination in breach of the duties on its maker, on the reading chosen` interp `the entity` `the public benefit determination`

@ref Article 5(1)(b), Article 7 (src:149) (src:203-213)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
      `the public benefit determination` IS A `Determination of public benefit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7 a determination in breach of the duties on its maker, on the reading chosen` interp `the entity` `the public benefit determination` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `what follows from a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker`
    WHEN `the determination does not answer the question`
        THEN `a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit`
    WHEN `the finding of the determination stands`
        THEN `Art 7 the determination finds public benefit as Article 5(1)(b) asks` `the entity` `the public benefit determination`
    WHEN `the entity is treated as not providing public benefit`
        THEN FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `Article 7(4) — Guidance on public benefit`

-- src:213 | (4) The guidance published by the Commissioner under Article 5(4), must in particular give guidance on the determination of the question of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit.
@ref Article 7(4) (src:213)
@export Whether the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on the determination of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit, as Article 7(4) requires; the input is the list of subjects the guidance covers
GIVEN subjects IS A LIST OF `Subject of the Commissioner's guidance`
        @desc The subjects on which the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 7(4) the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on public benefit` subjects MEANS
    elem `the determination of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit` subjects
